  "interpretation": "b < 0 means the margin decays as a power of log N; the criterion is never violated in the tested range, and a power-law decay never reaches zero in finite log N, so the fit gives NO finite crossing point -- an important negative result: the Nicolas margin is not heading to zero at any locatable place.",
